            <ArticleTitle>Primary ovarian echinococcosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The incidence of genital system hydatid disease in abdominal operation is 0.1%. During a period of 20 years (1957-1977), 12 cases were reported. This disease has no specific symptoms and findings. It is diagnosed intraoperatively.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">We report a 50-year-old patient admitted to our hospital with the complaint of abdominal pain and swelling, operated because of her adnexal mass and diagnosed as primary ovarian hydatid disease (echinococcosis).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
